The wbft-spec repository is licensed by path. The machine-readable form of
this mapping is REUSE.toml (REUSE specification 3.3, https://reuse.software);
the license texts are in LICENSES/.

1. The specification documents and the test vectors are licensed under the
   Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC-BY-4.0,
   LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt). This covers:

     README.md
     spec/          except spec/tools/
     spec-ko/       including spec-ko/tools/ (documentation only)
     spec/vectors/  (the conformance test vectors)

2. The programs under spec/tools/ (the vector generator, its checkers and
   adapter, and the drafting tools) are licensed under the GNU Lesser General
   Public License, version 3 or (at your option) any later version
   (LGPL-3.0-or-later, LICENSES/LGPL-3.0-or-later.txt). The LGPL incorporates
   the terms of the GNU General Public License version 3, whose text is in
   LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt. Every Go and Python source file under
   spec/tools/ carries an SPDX-License-Identifier line; the other files under
   spec/tools/ (go.mod, go.sum, JSON and TSV data, READMEs) are covered by
   REUSE.toml. Following the REUSE FAQ for projects under the LGPL-3.0,
   REUSE.toml marks one file, spec/tools/vectorgen/go.mod, as
   "LGPL-3.0-or-later OR GPL-3.0-or-later", so that the GPL text in
   LICENSES/ is referenced.

The tools build against go-stablenet (https://github.com/stable-net/go-stablenet),
which is itself licensed under the LGPL-3.0 and GPL-3.0. go-stablenet is not
part of this repository.
